        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{7}{9}$ compares shaded cells with unshaded cells. There are 16 cells altogether, so the shaded fraction of the whole is $\\frac{7}{16}$.",
          "worked": "$\\frac{7}{9}$ compares the 7 shaded cells with the 9 unshaded cells, rather than with the whole.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Total cells}&=7+9\\\\&=16\\\\\\text{Shaded fraction of the whole}&=\\frac{7}{16}\\end{align*}$$\nThe part-to-whole ratio is $7:16$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
